From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: ./sbt: drop `--jvm 11`, forward args to sbt

Two upstream papercuts in the same three-line script:

(1) `--jvm 11` makes Coursier's launcher fetch JDK 11 ad-hoc.
    cports has openjdk17 / openjdk21 but no openjdk11, and the
    Adoptium / Zulu tarballs Coursier downloads are glibc-linked
    so they can't exec on Chimera anyway.  Drop the flag and let
    Coursier use the JDK at $JAVA_HOME (set to JDK 21 in the
    cports template).

(2) The script runs `coursier launch sbt` with no `"$@"` — any
    args (e.g. `cli/pack`) get swallowed before sbt sees them,
    leaving sbt sitting at its interactive `>` prompt forever.
    Forward args after `--` so coursier passes them to the
    launched sbt main.

diff --git a/sbt b/sbt
--- a/sbt
+++ b/sbt
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 #!/usr/bin/env sh
 set -eu
-./bin/coursier launch --jvm 11 sbt
+./bin/coursier launch sbt -- "$@"
